      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The book, *Heart of Darkness*, follows Marlow's journey up the Congo River to a trading post, observing the brutal exploitation of the local people by European companies. The narrative is a descent into the moral decay of colonialism, where the supposed \"civilizing mission\" masks savage greed. The depiction of the Congolese people is often dehumanizing, serving primarily as a backdrop against which the European characters' moral failings and savagery are highlighted. It portrays them as primitive obstacles to European progress, which is a very common, and deeply problematic, trope of the era.",
